+## Revision 4: operator custody, accepted F-23 with owner amendment (2026-10-12)
+
+R-OPERATOR makes `swarma-operator` the no-harness broker operator/account owner and user-manager `operator` UID, with the broker software root outside session accounts. The phone-first, signed exact-act path and password-authenticated terminal fallback gate writes; mandatory `swarma-observer` serves confirmation-free reads. These are CIP-0011 slice-0 acceptance conditions, with device-key lifecycle and operator formats still open. CIPs stay Draft.
+
 ## Revision 3: accepted cycle-2 alignment (2026-10-12)
 
 R-SESSION/F-20 refines R-START: session lifecycle authorisation, a session-scoped host admission permit, per-physical-start claim/fence/receipt interlocks and `host_stop`. R-WORKPLACE/F-19 requires service-principal `swarma-rb-exec`, a relay-only `workplace` account class and project helper v1 qualification for every donor variant. CIP-0011 carries F-15 recovery controls, R-REBIND, R-TIME, R-SVC-EGRESS and the R-NETBIND reference to N15 (under review, not yet landed); F-16 keeps cross-account Git administration standalone. All unpublished formats and qualification gates stay open.
