+## Operator authority boundary
+
+[R-OPERATOR in CIP-0011 §5](CIP-0011-credential-broker-and-agent-users.md#5-curator-broker) governs the operator principal and its acts, including direct operator-UID mutations. Widening means grant issue, subscription enrolment, `team/1`, standing retirement or re-creation, explicit home retention, maintenance stop authority and renewal of standing grants. Revocation and account disabling require authentication only; phone revocation is one biometric confirmation and every phone act is displayed and signed. Status, grants, accounts and bindings reads use `swarma-observer` without confirmation. Existing delegated agent actions stay within their ceiling and never run under `swarma-operator`; `NOPASSWD` remains only for dispatcher service helper/launcher rules. The device key stays in the phone, while the unchanged-algorithm v0 software root remains protected in the separate operator account. No additional hardware is required for the terminal fallback. Loss of operator/root authority follows fenced root replacement, never restoration into a session account.
+
